---
# Focused on bug-finding and security-relevant checks, not style - this
# project has its own established K&R/tabs style (see CONTRIBUTING.md) that
# would conflict with readability-*/google-*/llvm-* naming and formatting
# checks, so those are deliberately not enabled.
#
# Disabled individual checks, and why:
#  - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: mostly fires on this project's own
#    consistent (subject, issuer, cn, is_ca, ...) constructor-style
#    functions; not a real bug pattern here.
#  - bugprone-narrowing-conversions: fires on every `int_field * 0.02f`
#    (spacenavd axis values are ints, sensitivity math is intentionally
#    float) - correct, intended code, not a bug.
#  - clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding: struct client's few bytes of
#    padding are irrelevant next to its megabyte-sized message buffers.
#  - clang-analyzer-security.ArrayBound: false positive on origins.c's
#    NULL-terminated-array loop (`for(i=0; allowed_origins[i]; i++)`) - the
#    analyzer doesn't track that the loop condition itself prevents ever
#    indexing past the NULL sentinel. Verified by manual inspection.
#    A `// NOLINTNEXTLINE` comment on that line does not suppress this
#    particular analyzer diagnostic reliably, hence disabling it here
#    instead - it's a single-purpose, 8-line file, so the loss of this
#    check elsewhere is negligible.
#  - cert-err33-c: flags every snprintf/fprintf/fflush return value as
#    "must be checked". For the truncation-tolerant, fixed-size-buffer
#    snprintf calls used throughout this project for paths/log messages, a
#    truncated string is a cosmetic issue, not a security one - checking
#    every call site would be many dozens of `(void)` casts for no real
#    safety gain. (ws_compute_accept()'s one snprintf where truncation could
#    matter already has its own explicit length check, unrelated to this
#    lint rule.)
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding,
  -clang-analyzer-security.ArrayBound,
  cert-*,
  -cert-err33-c,
  -cert-err34-c,
  performance-*,
  portability-*
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: 'src/.*\.h'
FormatStyle: none
